{
  "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
  "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In this admiralty case, the Eleventh Circuit held that Chatham County, a political subdivision of the State of Georgia, is entitled to sovereign immunity in Federal court. That is wrong for at least two reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Can a county be an arm of the State for some things?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: The question presented is -- is only sovereign immunity, isn't it? It's -- we don't have to decide whether there might be some other type of immunity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Who pays judgments? Who pays judgments against the county?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HART: Who pays judgments against the county is initially probably the county, but under Georgia law, the department of DOT -- Department of Transportation has a fund in which they can contribute towards that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Well, core -- core government functions isn't -- isn't the test either. I mean --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HART: Yes, sir. And there's strong case law, the Millwood case, that says basically counties are part of the sovereign of the State."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0001-0007",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One of the things that has been argued by the Solicitor General is that there's a single sovereign immunity, that there's this unified sovereign immunity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What about the South Carolina Supreme Court's opinion in the Hines case which seems to run counter to your argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: The -- the Eleventh Circuit had a prior decision, didn't they?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: That was an old Fifth Circuit case --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hart",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What we're asking here today is basically a very narrow holding. We're asking that there be limited sovereign immunity -- there -- excuse me -- that there be -- in unique circumstances where core functions of the State are delegated to the county, that the county would have sovereign immunity, and that a State can cloak a county with sovereign immunity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: It's not unusual that counties maintain and run bridges in your State, is it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hart",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "seems that that is an issue that the State ought to be able to do out of its delegation -- out of its dignity function. They ought to have the right to run the State and -- and delegate those functions as they see fit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hart",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "position there that -- that that is a core sovereign function, that the navigable waters are a sovereign interest of the State, and that should have the dignity and respect of that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Estrada",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On the issue that was raised by Justice Alito, the -- this doctrine comes from the Wickman case from the old Fifth Circuit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Estrada",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If that fact -- scenario were to come up in Chatham County and the plaintiffs and the defendants were diverse, there is no question that -- that the county would be entitled to plead its State law immunity under Erie."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Estrada",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You may recall that such a distinction between core and non-core governmental functions was at the core of the -- of this -- this Court's cases under National League of Cities v. Usery, and in the Garcia case, the Court overruled National League of Cities primarily on the point that the distinction between core and non-core governmental functions had proven to be unworkable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Estrada",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e827b9099939ef9ef6184bb59b946a5aedb7d697945f4b1b77ff775782aeda79",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e827b9099939-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think it's -- it's sort of inherent in all of the cases that have been ruled upon, Mr. Chief Justice, that what tends to be delegated are those that are the normal functions of government, but I don't think this Court has ever held that it is the function of sovereign immunity doctrine to tell the States what are the appropriate functions of government."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
